[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846510304","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-2846510304","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":2846510304,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pqkzg","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T06:59:06Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T07:30:42Z","body":"Alternative just off top of my head, don't know if this is doable:\r\n* Each new class type registers itself with `Manager` using classname and gets allotted an increasing ID\r\n* Ask the `Manager` not the class whether an object is / derived from classname\r\n* `Manager` creates bitfields for each class, if there are 200 classes in all, each bitfield is 200 bits, sets 1 if a member of that ID\r\n* For lookup, look up the ID in hashtable for the classname, then check the bitfield of the Object that is being queried.\r\n\r\nThat should be a hashtable lookup, and a bit check.\r\n\r\nEssentially I'm wondering if the `vector` can be replaced by a bitfield, and then check by ID instead of iterating through the `vector`. :thinking: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846510304/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846960212","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-2846960212","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":2846960212,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6psSpU","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T11:09:34Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T11:12:03Z","body":"> Alternative just off top of my head, don't know if this is doable:\r\n> \r\n> * Each new class type registers itself with `Manager` using classname and gets allotted an increasing ID\r\n> * Ask the `Manager` not the class whether an object is / derived from classname\r\n> * `Manager` creates bitfields for each class, if there are 200 classes in all, each bitfield is 200 bits, sets 1 if a member of that ID\r\n> * For lookup, look up the ID in hashtable for the classname, then check the bitfield of the Object that is being queried.\r\n> That should be a hashtable lookup, and a bit check.\r\n> \r\n> Essentially I'm wondering if the `vector` can be replaced by a bitfield, and then check by ID instead of iterating through the `vector`. 🤔\r\n\r\n`BitField` is unfortunately limited to the number of bits in whatever primitive you choose for it. A `BitField<uint64_t>` can only store 64 independent states (i.e. hold 64 classes). Since GDExtensions can register `GDCLASS` as well, it would need to be variable length (i.e. heap allocated).\r\nThere are around 1700 `GDCLASS` in Godot alone, so it would necessitate this 'variable' `BitField` to be at least 212 bytes long. This wouldn't be any better than the ~32 bytes currently needed for a class with 3 superclasses (e.g. `Object` -> `Node` -> `Node3D` -> `Path3D`).\r\n\r\nIndirection is also a notable concern: The current system identifies each class uniquely with a `constexpr void *`. To check for subclasses, you need 3 indirections (`object->gdtype->identifier_hierarchy->void *` identifiers) (notably, moving `is_class_ptr` to this system is planned for a follow-up PR). With a `Manager` system, you'd need several more: `object->gdtype->dynamic_bitfield` + `manager->hashmap->...->dynamic_bitfield`.\r\n\r\nThe main reason I want to get rid of this extensive `ClassDB` / manager system in the first place is to remove these layers of indirection, and just let objects know their own type as directly as possible :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846960212/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846982029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-2846982029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":2846982029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6psX-N","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T11:22:13Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T11:22:13Z","body":"> BitField is unfortunately limited to the number of bits in whatever primitive you choose for it. A BitField<uint64_t> can only store 64 independent states (i.e. hold 64 classes). Since GDExtensions can register GDCLASS as well, it would need to be variable length (i.e. heap allocated).\r\n\r\nYup, sure, e.g. `BitfieldDynamic` (we have one in 3.x).\r\n\r\n> There are around 1700 GDCLASS in Godot alone, so it would necessitate this 'variable' BitField to be at least 212 bytes long. This wouldn't be any better than the ~32 bytes currently needed for a class with 3 superclasses (e.g. Object -> Node -> Node3D -> Path3D).\r\n\r\nAh maybe that would be the clincher, I didn't realize we had so many GDCLASSes. :grin:\r\n\r\nBut maybe as we mentioned a while back, we could have a parallel simple faster bit check available for classes derived from `Spatial`, `CanvasItem` etc, so it would get the best of both worlds.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846982029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846995967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-2846995967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":2846995967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6psbX_","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T11:30:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T11:30:57Z","body":"> > BitField is unfortunately limited to the number of bits in whatever primitive you choose for it. A BitField<uint64_t> can only store 64 independent states (i.e. hold 64 classes). Since GDExtensions can register GDCLASS as well, it would need to be variable length (i.e. heap allocated).\r\n> \r\n> Yup, sure, e.g. `BitfieldDynamic` (we have one in 3.x).\r\n> \r\n> > There are around 1700 GDCLASS in Godot alone, so it would necessitate this 'variable' BitField to be at least 212 bytes long. This wouldn't be any better than the ~32 bytes currently needed for a class with 3 superclasses (e.g. Object -> Node -> Node3D -> Path3D).\r\n> \r\n> Ah maybe that would be the clincher, I didn't realize we had so many GDCLASSes. 😁\r\n> \r\n> But maybe as we mentioned a while back, we could have a parallel simple faster bit check available for classes derived from `Spatial`, `CanvasItem` etc, so it would get the best of both worlds.\r\n\r\nAgreed, that's definitely worth checking for performance benefits!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2846995967/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906876215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-2906876215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":2906876215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tQ2k3","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T14:57:35Z","updated_at":"2025-05-25T14:48:58Z","body":"Just a little update, I was able to use `ClassInfo` directly in `Object`, instead of introducing a new `GDType`. This ended up being a much more fully featured implementation. However, it also require some fixes to main registering order. \r\n\r\nIn the end, it makes more sense to build around and optimize existing systems than to introduce a new one next to it. I'll probably close this pull request, open the other implementation as a draft, and try to slowly build towards it with the changes mentioned above split into smaller, incremental packages.\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106646 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106775 are good first steps forwards, in any case.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906876215/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3154163194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-3154163194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":3154163194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68ALX6","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-05T08:51:37Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T08:51:37Z","body":"> Just a little update, I was able to use `ClassInfo` directly in Object, instead of introducing a new `GDType`.\r\n\r\nI think there's value in both approaches there. Migrating to a new `GDType` forces re-assessment of the structures used by `ClassInfo` to see if they are really the best fit. Reusing `ClassInfo` gets us some familiarity due to existing systems. It's hard to say what will work best here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3154163194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3154175255","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-3154175255","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":3154175255,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68AOUX","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-05T08:55:00Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T08:55:00Z","body":"> > Just a little update, I was able to use `ClassInfo` directly in Object, instead of introducing a new `GDType`.\r\n> \r\n> I think there's value in both approaches there. Migrating to a new `GDType` forces re-assessment of the structures used by `ClassInfo` to see if they are really the best fit. Reusing `ClassInfo` gets us some familiarity due to existing systems. It's hard to say what will work best here.\r\n\r\nRe-assessing `ClassInfo` is probably a worthy goal, but we can approach it separately and make incremental improvements, rather than trying to replace it with a new system entirely. I'm a believer in refactoring over rewriting, most times anyway :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3154175255/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3172264911","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-3172264911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":3172264911,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69FOvP","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-10T00:38:41Z","updated_at":"2025-08-10T00:38:41Z","body":"Incremental improvements tend to be the way to go. Though, on the merits, I think `GDType` is a better name, and moving to it (from `ClassInfo`) acts as a forcing function for that reassessment _and_ as a forcing function for something I mentioned in one of the earlier threads - `\"Pass the GDType around and do stuff with that directly\"`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3172264911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3357274029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-3357274029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":3357274029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IG--t","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T16:54:10Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T16:54:10Z","body":"Discussed in the Core meeting. We want to go ahead with adding a new `GDType` rather than adapting the existing `ClassInfo` from `ClassDB`. Functionality will slowly be moved over to `GDType`, redesigning when needed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3357274029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3371902306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105793#issuecomment-3371902306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105793","id":3371902306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7I-yVi","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-06T14:14:02Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T14:14:02Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3371902306/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]